so you're interested in signing up your  child for holiday class with the British  Council I think you're interested to  find out exactly what happens on each  day on the course well let's start with  day one on the first day of course all  the children arrive early in the morning  to meet their teachers for the first  time this is a very important moment in  the day because it's the first time when  they're going to really be introduced to  all of the different staff they'll be  working with them we have young learner  assistance coordinators and of course  the teachers who will teach their  classes the first day is very important  to get the children settled and  comfortable in their new classroom with  their new teachers the teachers will  begin the lessons very much centered on  trying to find out as much information  they can about them to get to know them  but also to assess their level to see if  any of them already have a little  English or not after this the teacher  may introduce for the first time the  story that they're going to be learning  that week the teacher might look at  introducing some new vocab that will be  important to understanding the story  also it's very important that they build  up a portfolio of work that they work on  through the whole week on the first day  they will often design their own covers  for their portfolios and this is a where  they will record all of their work  throughout each of the days day two at  the beginning of the day they usually  will review some of the language that  they learned on the first day  very this is an opportunity to see how  well they've understood and they can  recall some of the key verbs that are  going to be in the story later this can  be done through flashcards they will  teach them some little review games that  they can play together in the class and  again this might be the opportunity on  the second day for them to introduce the  story for the first time the word house  started wealthy this might be an  opportunity for the teacher to actually  show them the story and get them to  interact with the teacher throughout the  story to ask questions and learn more  about the story as they go on again this  is a very important part of the course  to develop their confidence to be able  to move on to using more complex  language later  moving on to day three by this point the  children have already started to take  some of the language on this is a moment  when the teacher might decide finally to  extend the language a little bit further  depending on the age or the level of the  class the teacher will look at more  complex language adjectives maybe verbs  or maybe some grammar structures that  will help them recite some actions and  some of the main events of the story  again if there will usually be  worksheets and some maybe little mini  games which the students will get  involved in and this is an opportunity  really for the teacher to become less  the main focus of the lesson and the  activities become more learner centered  now day four day 4 is already way over  halfway into the course and the children  have really start to develop their  understanding and their confidence to  use English at this point you start to  learn some more longer complex sentences  and phrases that are linked to the story  this is also the day when it becomes  important for the teacher to assign the  roles for the presentations that they're  going to do in the final day this will  be a chance for them to decide who is  going to play which role to enable them  to retell and recite the story for their  parents  another thing that's very important here  is for the teachers to be able to work  with them to improve their pronunciation  there's a lot of longer more complex  language at this point and this is  definitely a chance for the teacher to  work on them to help them in fine tune  their pronunciation to make it sound as  fluent as possible here we are on the  final day of the course of course this  is a day when the children have been  working towards the whole week this is  definitely the chance for the teacher to  really check to knows their roles and  can they really recite the story there  will be several practice sessions with  their teacher and the coordinators will  go through the whole of their story and  the song that they've been learning that  week as well what's very important to  remember at these three things firstly  the whole week takes place in English  from their classes with the English  teacher and also their outdoor games to  their art project but also very  importantly when they're on break times  or at lunch with our young learn  resistance everything takes place in  English secondly very important to know  that young children take time it takes  time for them to internalize all of this  English that they're hearing sometimes  for the first time and it will take time  for some of them to start producing and  develop their confidence to start using  English throughout the week further we  aim to create a positive learning  environment which is engaging for all of  the children from the very young ones to  the older ones this is very important  because this is the basis on which we  can teach them English and enable them  to engage and really have a love for  learning English and get the most out of  this type of course we look forward to  seeing you on the next course opening  very soon  [Music]
 

